                  "text": "Ps 31.13",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " On the morrow, when Pashhur released Jeremiah from the stocks, Jeremiah said to him, “The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.20.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.20.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " does not call your name Pashhur, but Terror on every side. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.20.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.20.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 20:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For thus says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.20.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.20.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ": Behold, I will make you a terror to yourself and to all your friends. They shall fall by the sword of their enemies while you look on. And I will give all Judah into the hand of the king of Babylon; he shall carry them captive to Babylon, and shall slay them with the sword. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.20.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.20.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 20:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moreover, I will give all the wealth of the city, all its gains, all its prized belongings, and all the treasures of the kings of Judah into the hand of their enemies, who shall plunder them, and seize them, and carry them to Babylon. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.20.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.20.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 20:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And you, Pashhur, and all who dwell in your house, shall go into captivity; to Babylon you shall go; and there you shall die, and there you shall be buried, you and all your friends, to whom you have prophesied falsely.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.20.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.20.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
